<title>USA: TABLE - Genesee &amp; Wyoming Q2 net income rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Genesee &amp; Wyoming Q2 net income rises.</headline>
<dateline>GREENWICH, Conn. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Genesee &amp; Yyoming Inc</p>
<p>			Three Months Ended    Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					June 30,		 June 30,</p>
<p>				    1997     1996	  1997     1996</p>
<p>OPERATING REVENUES	  23,479   19,009	47,571   35,618</p>
<p>OPERATING EXPENSES	  19,308   14,836	39,365   28,631</p>
<p>INCOME FROM OPERATIONS     4,171    4,173	 8,206    6,987</p>
<p>INTEREST EXPENSE	     (647)  (1,733)     (1,221)  (3,007)</p>
<p>OTHER INCOME		     100	180	  231	 261</p>
<p>NET INCOME		     2,157    1,559	 4,291    2,523</p>
<p>EARNINGS PER COMMON	  $0.40    $0.64	 $0.79    $1.05</p>
<p>WEIGHTED AVERAGE NUMBER OF</p>
<p>COMMON STOCK AND COMMON STOCK</p>
<p> EQUIVALENTS OUTSTANDING  5,440    2,444	 5,455     2,396</p>
<p>			 (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Company issued 3 million shares of common stock in an an initial public offering on June 24, 1996. Proceeds helped pay debt and lower interest expense by $1.1 million or 62.7 percent.</p>
<p>Latest results for quarter and six months reflect activity from all 1996 acquisitions -- Illinois &amp; Midland Railroad, Pittsburg &amp; Shawmut Railroad, and Rail Link.</p>
<p>Increase in operating ratio in the second quarter of 1997 compared to 1996 due to the labor-intensive Rail Link operation and start-up costs incurred in connection with new contracts; and  a change in traffic mix, principally related to temporarily decreased coal movements.</p>
</text>
